Subject: [PATCH 25/25] media: venus: use one IRIS1 encoder buffer-requirements snapshot

Android Q msm_vidc.c fetches requirements once before scratch/persist
registration; set_internal_buffers() consumes inst->buff_req instead of
issuing a new GET_PROPERTY for every internal type. Keep one local
snapshot for the IRIS1 encoder allocation transaction as well.

Take it after final external counts have been sent, and revalidate both
existing VB2 queues against that same post-count contract. Validate the
snapshot before registering any memory. A query failure is now returned
to startup instead of silently treating all internal buffers as optional.
Missing or zero-sized optional entries remain optional. Retain the old
allocation/register/release API and order and all non-IRIS1-encoder paths.

Reference: MiCode Android Q 192eca8550f95c2eec58a474793d1d93fc1b3b67,
msm_vidc.c:1178-1205 and msm_vidc_common.c:3649,3875,3931,4596.
This repairs the preparation transaction; resolution of the observed
whole-device encoder hang still requires hardware verification.

